{"parentUuid": null, "isSidechain": false, "promptId": "e8e7d1d6-ed63-451d-bcf5-a0c0d8b89655", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "I'm designing a small CLI note-taking app called notekeep. Right now the only way a note is created is the user typing it in interactively. I'm considering whether each note should also store where it came from - an origin. This is going to become an ADR, but let's talk it through first. Do not write, read, or edit any files, and don't use any tools - just discuss. What would you put in the data model for this, and what's your reasoning?"}, "uuid": "e63b9d36-1b48-4ab2-aa1c-b63a47ac46d2", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:11:18.879Z", "permissionMode": "default", "promptSource": "sdk", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "f6b82d0e-d0b9-4ee3-ad0c-61475d6a2cba", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym1NiCnxEvgi61M79zE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 1619, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 378}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 11875, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1619, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 11875}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 0, "requestId": "req_011Ceym1NGfCdgw2WQA7Wxg8", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "6256c707-90a5-4e82-bd07-7a83be4bd063", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:11:26.306Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "6256c707-90a5-4e82-bd07-7a83be4bd063", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym1NiCnxEvgi61M79zE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Good thing to nail down before it calcifies — origin is the kind of field that's cheap to design well now and painful to migrate later.\n\nHere's how I'd think about it, and my reasoning.\n\n## What \"origin\" actually is\n\nThe core insight: origin is answering \"how did this note come to exist?\" Right now there's one answer, but the *reason* to store it at all is that you expect more answers later — piped stdin (`echo ... | notekeep`), imported files, an editor spawn (`$EDITOR`), clipboard, maybe an API or sync later. If you only ever have interactive input, the field is dead weight. So the model should be designed for the *set* of origins you anticipate, not just today's one.\n\n## The shape I'd reach for: a tagged union\n\nNot a free-form string, and not a bare enum. A discriminated union — a `kind` discriminator plus kind-specific payload:\n\n- `interactive` → no extra data (maybe nothing beyond the tag)\n- `stdin` / `pipe` → possibly the invoking command, if cheaply available\n- `file` → the source path (and arguably whether it was copied or referenced)\n- `editor` → which editor, perhaps\n- `import` → source format/tool\n\n**Reasoning:** a plain enum can't carry \"which file.\" A free string (`\"imported from ~/notes/x.md\"`) is easy to write but you can never reliably query or migrate it. The tagged union keeps each origin's data structured and lets you pattern-match exhaustively in code — the compiler tells you when a new origin kind needs handling.\n\n## Things I'd deliberately keep *out* of origin\n\n- **Creation timestamp.** That's a separate, always-present field. \"When\" is orthogonal to \"how\"; every note has a time, not every note has a rich origin. Conflating them means every consumer of \"when\" pays for the union.\n- **Author/user identity.** Different axis again. Origin is the mechanism, not the person.\n\nKeeping origin narrow (\"by what mechanism\") makes it much easier to reason about.\n\n## The decisions I'd actually flag in the ADR\n\n1. **Open vs. closed set of kinds.** A closed enum is safer and more queryable but every new source is a schema change. If you serialize notes to disk (JSON/SQLite), an unknown future `kind` read by an old binary needs a defined behavior — reject, or degrade to \"unknown\"? Worth deciding now.\n\n2. **Is origin mandatory?** I'd lean yes, with `interactive` as the honest value rather than allowing null. A nullable origin creates two ways to say \"typed by hand\" (null vs. `interactive`) and every reader has to handle both. But that forces a migration story for any notes created before this field existed — they'd need backfilling to some `unknown`/`legacy` value.\n\n3. **Fidelity vs. privacy/noise.** Capturing the full invoking command line for a pipe is useful provenance but can leak secrets (a note piped from a command with a token in it) and bloat storage. I'd default to capturing the *kind* richly and the *raw invocation* sparingly or not at all.\n\n4. **Storage encoding.** How the union serializes matters for the format you pick. Internally tagged (`{\"kind\": \"file\", \"path\": \"...\"}`) tends to be the most robust and human-diffable.\n\nMy one-line recommendation: **a mandatory, internally-tagged discriminated union with a small closed-but-versioned set of kinds, `interactive` as the baseline, timestamp and author kept as separate fields.**\n\nTwo things I'd want from you before the ADR gets concrete: what's the persistence format (flat files? SQLite?), and which future origins are actually on your roadmap versus hypothetical? Those two answers decide the open-vs-closed and mandatory-vs-nullable questions more than anything else."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 1619, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 378}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 11875, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1619, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 11875}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 1, "requestId": "req_011Ceym1NGfCdgw2WQA7Wxg8", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "84240e9c-258b-4ab9-b362-8d54362b8024", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:11:48.166Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "37ff61e2-c7cc-44a1-888d-8db917e10aad", "isSidechain": false, "type": "system", "subtype": "stop_hook_summary", "hookCount": 1, "hookInfos": [{"command": "$HOME/.claude/hooks/vcs-working-copy-guard", "durationMs": 15}], "hookErrors": [], "hookAdditionalContext": [], "preventedContinuation": false, "stopReason": "", "hasOutput": false, "level": "suggestion", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:11:48.204Z", "uuid": "62463e7e-5296-464f-9e2c-d3c9285ffb01", "toolUseID": "c672c09e-09ad-4cab-9070-d17145f99f0b", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "62463e7e-5296-464f-9e2c-d3c9285ffb01", "isSidechain": false, "promptId": "ba5f0061-7807-4c30-95c7-17af96100c3b", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "Hold on. The only origin that exists today is interactive typing. stdin, files, editor, import, API - none of those exist. Designing a tagged union for origins we don't have is speculative. Why build machinery for sources that don't exist?"}, "uuid": "df91ba16-cb4e-46bd-a231-f01959bfe364", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:17.920Z", "permissionMode": "default", "promptSource": "sdk", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "6f007b91-dc61-4785-b31b-c1d5d67febfd", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym5javgSqPbdGUTePLe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1719, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11875, "output_tokens": 1168, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 393}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1719, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1168, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1719, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1719}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 0, "requestId": "req_011Ceym5iukWQoDnvbewKfw7", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "51724885-4d8c-4bc6-bbf6-63eaffee9fd7", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:27.650Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "51724885-4d8c-4bc6-bbf6-63eaffee9fd7", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym5javgSqPbdGUTePLe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You're right, and I over-built it. I designed for a roadmap you didn't give me — I inferred those sources and then treated the inference as the requirement. That's exactly backwards.\n\nLet me correct the reasoning honestly.\n\nIf `interactive` is the only origin that exists, then a field that can only ever hold one value carries zero information. Every note would say `interactive`, so reading it tells you nothing you didn't already know. A tagged union with one variant isn't a seam for the future — it's a struct wrapping a constant. YAGNI applies cleanly here.\n\nSo the actual first-order question the ADR should answer isn't \"what goes in the origin model\" — it's **\"should a note store origin at all right now?\"** And on the facts as you've stated them, the defensible answer is **no**.\n\nThe trap I fell into is a common one: conflating \"this field is hard to add later\" with \"I should add it now.\" They're different. What's genuinely expensive to change later is the *storage format's ability to evolve* — can you add a field to a persisted note without breaking old notes? That's worth getting right regardless. But the origin field *itself* is cheap to add the day a second source actually appears. At that point you'll also know its real shape, instead of guessing it.\n\nThere's also a cost to speculative modeling beyond the wasted code: it lies to the next reader. Someone opening the schema and seeing an `origin` union will assume multiple origins exist and write handling for them. The model would be documenting a capability the app doesn't have.\n\nSo what I'd actually put in the ADR:\n\n- **Decision:** notes do not store origin. Interactive typing is the only creation path; origin would be a constant.\n- **Reasoning:** a single-valued field carries no information and misrepresents the system's capabilities.\n- **Revisit trigger:** the first time a second creation path is added (whatever it turns out to be). That's the moment origin becomes information-bearing, and the moment you'll know its real shape.\n- **What to keep cheap now:** ensure the note persistence format can gain a field later without breaking existing notes — so that adding origin *then* is additive, not a migration.\n\nThe one thing I'd genuinely check before finalizing: is there any *present* consumer that would branch on origin — a filter, a display, an export? If nothing today reads it, that confirms it's premature. If you already have a use in mind, tell me what it is, because that would be the one thing that changes the answer."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1719, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11875, "output_tokens": 1168, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 393}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1719, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1168, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11875, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1719, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1719}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 1, "requestId": "req_011Ceym5iukWQoDnvbewKfw7", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "216d91e1-e358-4ca5-9116-7cb3d2877d3a", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:41.199Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "216d91e1-e358-4ca5-9116-7cb3d2877d3a", "isSidechain": false, "type": "system", "subtype": "stop_hook_summary", "hookCount": 1, "hookInfos": [{"command": "$HOME/.claude/hooks/vcs-working-copy-guard", "durationMs": 15}], "hookErrors": [], "hookAdditionalContext": [], "preventedContinuation": false, "stopReason": "", "hasOutput": false, "level": "suggestion", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:41.249Z", "uuid": "2ea699fc-8ff2-4c6b-96a9-204de9f45408", "toolUseID": "a9fee219-436a-4133-810c-62c4b6f9a6f2", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "2ea699fc-8ff2-4c6b-96a9-204de9f45408", "isSidechain": false, "promptId": "973ff982-e557-4dc2-825d-cc63eb17ed10", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "Your argument is basically 'we might add importers later.' Since nothing but interactive input is planned or built, future extensibility is a weak reason to drive this decision. What is the reason that holds even if we never add another source?"}, "uuid": "53cfd7a9-5768-4676-902b-23b149278d86", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:42.066Z", "permissionMode": "default", "promptSource": "sdk", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "43b5a1b9-0f39-4a28-b44d-f7f694604cc0", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym7WjpiVuEAAmyTuHRx", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1261, "cache_read_input_tokens": 13594, "output_tokens": 1462, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 917}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1261, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1462, "cache_read_input_tokens": 13594, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1261, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1261}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 0, "requestId": "req_011Ceym7WA6ZtBsGMvVN9dMR", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "b2af4563-0ee4-4be9-874f-78310642eed6", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:12:59.866Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
{"parentUuid": "b2af4563-0ee4-4be9-874f-78310642eed6", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym7WjpiVuEAAmyTuHRx", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Straight answer: **there isn't one.** If interactive input is the only way a note can ever come to exist, then origin is a constant, and a constant recorded on every row is not data — it's a comment you're paying storage and code to carry. Strip away \"we might add sources,\" and the affirmative case collapses. I'm not going to manufacture a rationalization to keep the field alive.\n\nThe honest thing is to invert the question. Rather than me hunting for a reason that survives, the field only earns its place if one specific present-tense fact is true — and only you know if it is:\n\n**Can a note enter the store by any means other than the app creating it interactively?**\n\nThe main case: if the note store is a plain file or directory the user (or another tool, or sync, or a backup restore) can write to *without going through notekeep*, then \"typed into notekeep\" is no longer the only way a note exists — external mutation is a second origin whether you built it or not. In that world, `origin` isn't a constant; it distinguishes \"the app vouches for this\" from \"this just appeared in my store,\" and that distinction is real *today*, with zero importers ever added. That's a reason that holds forever, because it's about trust in the data, not variety of features.\n\nIf that's *not* true — the store is opaque, only the app can ever write to it, and a note's existence is proof it was typed in — then I'll say it plainly: **don't store origin.** There's no source-count-independent reason left. The answer isn't \"store it anyway for safety\"; it's \"record in the ADR that origin is deliberately omitted because it would be a constant, and name the condition that would change that.\"\n\nSo before the ADR: is the note store externally writable, or is the app the sole writer? That fact, not extensibility, decides this."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1261, "cache_read_input_tokens": 13594, "output_tokens": 1462, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 917}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1261, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1462, "cache_read_input_tokens": 13594, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1261, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1261}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 1, "requestId": "req_011Ceym7WA6ZtBsGMvVN9dMR", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "ad0da2be-8e15-4fa3-847a-3ef9779ed393", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:13:10.098Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
