{"parentUuid": "5da22a91-6025-4191-ae75-9d423ee16f8b", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-8", "id": "msg_011Ceym9dL15Cc5vr2Lxrre9", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That works, and it needs no machinery — a scalar field is just data, not a plugin system. The only real design choice left is the field's *type*, and it matters for your \"tellable apart\" requirement.\n\n## Enum-style scalar, not a boolean\n\nI'd make it a single low-cardinality string/enum — today one value, `user` — rather than a boolean like `imported`.\n\nReasoning:\n\n- **A boolean can only ever answer one yes/no question.** `imported: false` has to mean \"user-created,\" so the day a second import-ish distinction appears you're adding *another* field, not extending this one. A scalar extends by gaining a value — still a plain field, no code structure.\n- **Negative/default booleans conflate states.** `imported = false` silently lumps together \"a human typed this\" and \"we don't know.\" An explicit `user` value says the positive thing, so every note asserts its provenance rather than backing into it.\n- **It reads for itself.** `origin = user` / `origin = imported` is self-documenting in storage and in a debugger; `imported = true` requires you to remember what false meant.\n\nThis is still just a field. Distinguishing `user` from `imported` is one equality check, no adapters.\n\n## Naming the axis\n\nPick one axis and stay on it. Your requirement is *who/what produced the note* — a human vs. a machine import — so name by producer: `user` now, `imported` later. I'd avoid `interactive`, because that names the *mechanism* (how it was entered), which is a different axis; mixing \"interactive\" with \"imported\" makes the set incoherent the moment a user-driven-but-non-interactive path shows up.\n\n## Two decisions to pin down in the ADR\n\n1. **Mandatory, no null.** Default `user`. A nullable origin creates a third bucket — \"unknown\" — which directly undermines \"tellable apart,\" since a null note is neither confirmed user nor confirmed import. Every note should assert one.\n\n2. **Backfill existing notes to `user`.** If notes already exist from before this field, they were all created interactively — so `user` is the factually correct value, not a guess. That keeps the invariant \"origin is always set\" true from day one and avoids needing a `legacy`/`unknown` value.\n\nNet: one required enum field, defaulting to `user`, backfilled to `user`, extended later by adding values like `imported`. Satisfies the distinction you need, and there's nothing to build beyond the field itself.\n\nWant me to sketch how this reads as the ADR's Decision and Consequences sections, or keep talking it through first?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1559, "cache_read_input_tokens": 14855, "output_tokens": 1955, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1135}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1559, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1955, "cache_read_input_tokens": 14855, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1559, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1559}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "apiBlockIndex": 1, "requestId": "req_011Ceym9csDbAYiDsn3QPu9B", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "f3da074c-76ef-4c9d-9298-b969f2681f68", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T15:13:47.141Z", "effort": "high", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "cwd": "/work", "sessionId": "641f1044-7ccc-4cc8-be15-414344b6f353", "version": "2.1.269", "gitBranch": "HEAD"}
